1307,"bookmarkCount":4,"language":"en","possiblySensitive":false,"topic":"verification-evals"},{"id":"2028961906900549768","createdAt":"2026-03-03T22:33:09+00:00","author":"poteto","displayName":"lauren","profilePicture":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2093473719830315008/oo09g1Ov_normal.jpg","type":"post","isQuote":false,"text":"in the next version of noodle\n\nall you need to install and get a working noodle loop is to paste a prompt to your agent. it will learn from your past conversations to build a workflow thats tailored for your repo.\n\ntry it: \n\n𝙸𝚗𝚜𝚝𝚊𝚕𝚕 𝙽𝚘𝚘𝚍𝚕𝚎 𝚊𝚗𝚍 𝚜𝚎𝚝 𝚞𝚙 𝚝𝚑𝚒𝚜 𝚙𝚛𝚘𝚓𝚎𝚌𝚝. 𝙵𝚘𝚕𝚕𝚘𝚠\n𝚑𝚝𝚝𝚙𝚜://𝚛𝚊𝚠.𝚐𝚒𝚝𝚑𝚞𝚋𝚞𝚜𝚎𝚛𝚌𝚘𝚗𝚝𝚎𝚗𝚝.𝚌𝚘𝚖/𝚙𝚘𝚝𝚎𝚝𝚘/𝚗𝚘𝚘𝚍𝚕𝚎/𝚖𝚊𝚒𝚗/𝙸𝙽𝚂𝚃𝙰𝙻𝙻.𝚖𝚍","url":"https://x.com/poteto/status/2028961906900549768","conversationId":"2028961906900549768","inReplyToId":"","inReplyToUsername":"","quotedPost":null,"media":[{"id":"2028961232221552640","type":"photo","url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HChRfaWawAAoIGD.jpg","width":3584,"height":2004,"altText":""}],"externalUrl":"","likeCount":54,"replyCount":3,"retweetCount":2,"quoteCount":1,"viewCount":5231,"bookmarkCount":37,"language":"en","possiblySensitive":false},{"id":"2028958009565823209","createdAt":"2026-03-03T22:17:40+00:00","author":"poteto","displayName":"lauren","profilePicture":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2093473719830315008/oo09g1Ov_normal.jpg","type":"reply","isQuote":false,"text":"@fat super nice! going to integrate diffs into noodle's ui\n\nhttps://t.co/iXJNxy8hOa","url":"https://x.com/poteto/status/2028958009565823209","conversationId":"2028950411626111359","inReplyToId":"2028950411626111359","inReplyToUsername":"fat","quotedPost":null,"media":[],"externalUrl":"https://github.com/poteto/noodle/blob/main/brain/plans/86-diffs-integration/overview.md","likeCount":5,"replyCount":1,"retweetCount":0,"quoteCount":0,"viewCount":1058,"bookmarkCount":3,"language":"en","possiblySensitive":false},{"id":"2028947604252553650","createdAt":"2026-03-03T21:36:19+00:00","author":"poteto","displayName":"lauren","profilePicture":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2093473719830315008/oo09g1Ov_normal.jpg","type":"reply","isQuote":false,"text":"thanks @Apple https://t.co/dbm99yKfeR","url":"https://x.com/poteto/status/2028947604252553650","conversationId":"2028944652800540775","inReplyToId":"2028944652800540775","inReplyToUsername":"poteto","quotedPost":null,"media":[{"id":"2028947561353244672","type":"photo","url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HChFDqZa8AAq3kl.png","width":622,"height":226,"altText":""}],"externalUrl":"","likeCount":12,"replyCount":0,"retweetCount":0,"quoteCount":0,"viewCount":2023,"bookmarkCount":0,"language":"en","possiblySensitive":false},{"id":"2028944652800540775","createdAt":"2026-03-03T21:24:35+00:00","author":"poteto","displayName":"lauren","profilePicture":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2093473719830315008/oo09g1Ov_normal.jpg","type":"quote","isQuote":true,"text":"i really want to upgrade my 6 year old personal macbook. although one \"feature\" of having the old intel cpu is that i can quickly tell from the heat and the fans taking off when my code has perf issues lmao","url":"https://x.com/poteto/status/2028944652800540775","conversationId":"2028944652800540775","inReplyToId":"","inReplyToUsername":"","quotedPost":{"id":"2028857273578323984","author":"gregjoz","displayName":"Greg Joswiak","profilePicture":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1535411147087790081/5qbJDG-P_normal.jpg","text":"The all-new MacBook Pro with M5 Pro and M5 Max pushes the boundaries of what you can accomplish from anywhere.\n\nRun advanced large language models on device and unlock capabilities that can't be done on any other laptop—all while maintaining exceptional battery life! https://t.co/t3f3SQrFb9","createdAt":"2026-03-03T15:37:23+00:00","url":"https://x.com/gregjoz/status/2028857273578323984","media":[{"id":"2028854972243460096","type":"video","url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2028854972243460096/img/yTnhsn5m-qZZU-GG.jpg","width":1920,"height":1080,"altText":"","playbackUrl":"https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2028854972243460096/vid/avc1/1920x1080/9ifYI07Wz6dgfrKF.mp4?tag=21"}]},"media":[],"externalUrl":"","likeCount":41,"replyCount":5,"retweetCount":2,"quoteCount":0,"viewCount":6919,"bookmarkCount":3,"language":"en","possiblySensitive":false},{"id":"2028926690861433196","createdAt":"2026-03-03T20:13:13+00:00","author":"poteto","displayName":"lauren","profilePicture":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2093473719830315008/oo09g1Ov_normal.jpg","type":"reply","isQuote":false,"text":"@nandcello yeah that's why i use this https://t.co/03MkEOb2Py to tighten everything. i run it about once a week","url":"https://x.com/poteto/status/2028926690861433196","conversationId":"2028645625525596349","inReplyToId":"2028799427838931428","inReplyToUsername":"nandcello","quotedPost":null,"media":[],"externalUrl":"https://github.com/poteto/noodle/blob/main/.agents/skills/meditate/SKILL.md","likeCount":2,"replyCount":0,"retweetCount":0,"quoteCount":0,"viewCount":172,"bookmarkCount":4,"language":"en","possiblySensitive":false},{"id":"2028924706305524131","createdAt":"2026-03-03T20:05:20+00:00","author":"poteto","displayName":"lauren","profilePicture":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2093473719830315008/oo09g1Ov_normal.jpg","type":"post","isQuote":false,"text":"a useful principle i have in noodle's repo is encoding lessons in structure. asking agents to remember to do something doesn't work reliably. it needs to be structural if possible - whether in code or through static lints/hooks\n\nhttps://t.co/MUzqAA6PAl","url":"https://x.com/poteto/status/2028924706305524131","conversationId":"2028924706305524131","inReplyToId":"","inReplyToUsername":"","quotedPost":null,"media":[],"externalUrl":"https://github.com/poteto/noodle/blob/main/brain/principles/encode-lessons-in-structure.md","likeCount":37,"replyCount":2,"retweetCount":2,"quoteCount":0,"viewCount":2718,"bookmarkCount":31,"language":"en","possiblySensitive":false},{"id":"2028645625525596349","createdAt":"2026-03-03T01:36:22+00:00","author":"poteto","displayName":"lauren","profilePicture":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2093473719830315008/oo09g1Ov_normal.jpg","type":"post","isQuote":false,"text":"one of my most used skills\nhttps://t.co/A2gXeOD3l9","url":"https://x.com/poteto/status/2028645625525596349","conversationId":"2028645625525596349","inReplyToId":"","inReplyToUsername":"","quotedPost":null,"media":[],"externalUrl":"https://skills.sh/poteto/noodle/adversarial-review","likeCount":635,"replyCount":7,"retweetCount":27,"quoteCount":1,"viewCount":50854,"bookmarkCount":1013,"language":"en","possiblySensitive":false},{"id":"2028623132823892229","createdAt":"2026-03-03T00:06:59+00:00","author":"poteto","displayName":"lauren","profilePicture":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2093473719830315008/oo09g1Ov_normal.jpg","type":"reply","isQuote":false,"text":"4. noodle will soon support custom runtimes. today you get 2 options: either local processes, or https://t.co/lX5rRsD3q1. but there's no reason why we can't support any runtime. noodle runtime plugins will let you run your tasks anywhere: private cloud, mac mini, etc.","url":"https://x.com/poteto/status/2028623132823892229","conversationId":"2028608916129767582","inReplyToId":"2028622852325605766","inReplyToUsername":"poteto","quotedPost":null,"media":[],"externalUrl":"https://sprites.dev/","likeCount":2,"replyCount":2,"retweetCount":0,"quoteCount":0,"viewCount":854,"bookmarkCount":1,"language":"en","possiblySensitive":false},{"id":"2028622852325605766","createdAt":"2026-03-03T00:05:52+00:00","author":"poteto","displayName":"lauren","profilePicture":"https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2093473719830315008/oo09g1Ov_normal.jpg","type":"reply","isQuote":false,"text":"3. it's designed to be extremely hackable. noodle's state is all written to disk in a .noodle dir in your project. agents can read these files easily (and they do!) to understand what's going on